{
  "about": "The iPad's own rules of the playback model (v0.6.3, #608 item 3, the lead's decision reversing #521 5 on the iPad): while Цикл plays, a selection that appears or changes so that it does not hold the position takes playback to its start and loops it; one that holds it plays on; stopped, as the shared file has it. PlaybackPositionTests runs these in place of the shared cases named in 'replaces' (Golden/playback-model.json, which the web's reference runs unchanged). Since 0.8 (Andrei's answers 14 and 16, 2026-11-18, thread «Версия 0.7»): a tap on the score's beat, or the position kept with the notes' view put back ('place'), leaves Цикл on; outside the selection it is a lead-in ('leadIn'), from which Play plays into the selection, which then loops. The roll's taps stay T12 ('seek', the shared cases).",
  "replaces": [
    "changes with Цикл on: the new one loops, the position stays and is caught when playback reaches it",
    "changes away from the position with Цикл on: the position does not jump",
    "changes to behind the position while playing: the loop cannot catch it, so Цикл turns off (#521 5)",
    "appears while playing before it: Цикл on, the loop waits, the position stays",
    "appears while playing behind the position: Цикл stays off, nothing loops (#521 5)"
  ],
  "cases": [
